<title>UK: Transco UK gas forecasts for April 17.</title>
<headline>Transco UK gas forecasts for April 17.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transco, the pipeline and</p>
<p>transport arm of BG plc, has announced the following forecasts</p>
<p>and data for gas consumption in the period April 15 to 17.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = million cubic metres)</p>
<p>Apr 15 (actual) 211 mcm, 49 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Apr 16 (forecast) 212 mcm, 49 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Apr 17 (forecast) 213 mcm, 50 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>(SNT = seasonal normal temperature)</p>
<p>Apr 15 (actual) 8.2 Celsius, SNT 9.6 Celsius</p>
<p>Apr 16 (forecast) 9.4 Celsius, SNT 9.7 Celsius</p>
<p>Apr 17 (forecast) 8.9 Celsius, SNT 9.8 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no supply interruption called by Transco on Wednesday, with none forecast for Thursday.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
